INSERT INTO missionObjectives (missionID, briefingText) VALUES
(60131,'/h2> I''m happy to announce that we just spotted a transport ship owned by the Archaeological Agency of Caille University not far from a stargate in this system. It is being escorted by some rather menacing Navy ships, and therefore we''ve been a bit wary to attack it. I''m sure it got lost and took a wrong jump somewhere along its travel route, no sane captain of a civilian transport ship would travel through these parts on purpose. You probably guessed it but I''d like you to do the dirty work. Fly off to their current location and eliminate the escort. If the transport freighter puts up a fight then destroy it as well, but try to bring back as many of its passengers as you can. These civilian transport ships can be a goldmine for those in the kidnapping / ransom business, if you know what I mean. I''m sure the Gallenteans will pay a handsome amount of ISK for their precious archaeologists, if taken alive. </span'),
(60132,'/h2> Welcome back you. I''m excited here, we''re pretty sure that the passengers you captured in a previous mission are of a very wealthy or important family. We can''t say for certain yet, but there''s something about them ... Anyway, I''d like you to transfer a sample of their DNA to the destination, where Zunbar Alefon, our expert on Gallentean internal affairs, is located. Hopefully he will be able to find a match for them in his gigantic DNA database and give us some information on their backgrounds. And don''t tell ANYONE what you''re up to, I''d rather keep a low profile on this for the time being, the fewer members of the agent''s corporation that know about this the better. </span'),
(60133,'/h2> The morning prison guard shift met with a grisly scene. All of the guards on the 5th deck on the last shift had been brutally murdered and some of the prison cells had been forcibly opened. 2 of the prisoners that you captured in a previous mission were missing. We are quite certain that this was the work of a bounty hunter, as he obviously intended to rescue these specific prisoners. We immediately banned all craft from leaving the station, but it was too late. However we have compiled a list of those who left the station this morning and we''ve narrowed it down to 3 suspects. We know the location of each of them, they haven''t managed to leave the system yet. I''ll upload their locations one by one, do whatever it takes to bring back those prisoners! </span'),
(60134,'/h2> I received a response from Zunbar Alefon, the person that was supposed to identify the prisoners that you captured in a previous mission. Apparently, one of them is a very famous Gallente archaeologist, Karzath Pinazi, distantly related to Senator Tarek Pinazi! This is an incredible stroke of fortune for us, capturing a relative of a Gallente senator and famous icon is almost unheard of. I''ve no doubt that he will get us a mighty fine ransom. The only bad news is that this will probably bring a lot of bounty hunters into our backyard ... but hey, we have you to deal with that problem. Now, on to your assignment. I need you to go to the destination with a data chip that I''ll have dropped off into your hangar. This chip contains all of our demands towards the Gallente Federation in exchange for the release of the prisoners. In it, we also threaten them with the slaying of their dear archaeologist team if they dare to launch a full scale assault on our station. I''m pretty sure that will keep them at bay for the time being. </span'),
(60135,'/h2> After you delivered the data chip in your last mission, I''ve been flooded with reports of Gallente Navy sightings in the dungeon. A number of our gangs have been wiped out, and it''s not considered safe anymore for a pirate to venture too far out into space in these parts. I''m positive that this new offensive is the direct result of the data chip we sent falling into the hands of the Navy generals. They know what we''re up to and it''s only a matter of time before the Gallente media get a hold of the story. I didn''t expect the Navy to venture this close to our station, after all we''ve threatened to kill the prisoners. But they seem intent on keeping their distance, this is just a ploy of theirs to frighten us. But by disrupting our trade routes and ambushing our patrols in the dungeon, all they accomplish is raising the price on our demands. I want you to head out into the outer reaches of this system and eliminate 4 Navy groups. After we have given them the taste of defeat, then it will be time to deliver our new demands. Off you go. </span'),
(60069,'/h2> Your attack on the Navy groups has had unforeseeable consequences. Instead of backing off, they have taken their offensive to another level. We''ve noticed an unusually large concentration of their ships at a location within the dungeon, and a construction freight or two heading their way. We''re quite sure they are planning on building something there, probably a military outpost from which they intend to launch a major offensive against this station. We can''t let them start building that outpost! I want you to personally see to it that their convoy and all of the ships defending the area are destroyed immediately. </span'),
(60070,'/h2> Your last strike against the Navy forces in the agent''s system sent them into a disarray. That should keep them in check for a day or two. Meanwhile, I''d like you to bring our new demands to the destination. This time they better comply, or we might just go through with all of our threats. We''ve already decapitated one of the prisoners, which we believe to be a personal aid of Karzath. The footage has been compiled into the data disk along with our demands. </span'),
(60071,'/h2> I''m glad you''re back you. The Gallente Navy have gone mad! They''ve sent an entire fleet of ships to attack this station. They must be utterly insane, if even one of them steps foot in here the prisoners heads will roll! I need you to undock at once and meet the Navy head on before they get within firing range of the station, bring everyone you can, I suspect you''ll need all the help you can get. You''ll be supplied with a bookmark of course, now get moving! </span'),
(60072,'/h2> Rejoice, you, the Federation have finally caved in. They have vowed to meet our demands once the prisoner and his cargo have been transferred safely to the destination, where their agents will pick it up. Ironically enough, we have no idea what cargo they were jammering about, everything that was on board the cargo ship containing the archeologists you captured originally was destroyed along with the ship. No wonder they were so adamant at retrieving whatever it was they were after. Karzath Nuoki was only a smokescreen, whatever he was transporting towards Gallente space was extremely valuable. It''s unfortunate we will never find out what it was, as I''m sure you never saw anything suspicious in the wreckage of the cargo ship other than the stranded archeologists ... but just to be on the safe side, I had some of my men search your hangar just in case you have been less than honest with us. No hard feelings I hope. And as you probably guessed, I want you to do the honors of transporting the prisoner to the destination, where our agents will hand him along with a cargo container filled with various junk to our Gallente ''friends''. Once this final assignment has been completed, I ... err we will be able to enjoy the fruits of our hard work. In other words, I''ll be rich! </span'),
(60136,'/h2> A minor Amarrian noble has claimed ownership of a sizable portion of the dungeon, claiming one of his ancestors was given this part of space as a reward for his ancestor''s duties to the emperor. The area includes a couple of planets, their satellites, and an asteroid field. Anyway, this guy has now sent us an official warning that any aggression against "his" assets will be met with an iron fist. He completely underestimates our strength in the region, believing his small mercenary force sufficient to scare us off. Fly to the fool''s position and destroy the Control Tower he''s holding out there, along with the mercenary forces defending him. Let''s put this idiot out of his misery. </span'),
(60137,'/h2> Your successful attack on the Numon mercenary outpost seems to be sitting badly with certain factions in the Amarr Empire. A few members of the Sarum family have taken up Kazar''s cause, and they''ve already started mobilizing their personal fleets to make a trip here to get involved in our little territorial dispute. We''ve already sent out scan probes to collect data on any Imperial activity in the the agent''s region region. This data will be stored in a computer disc which I expect you to fetch for me at the pickup location. Once we retrieve this data we will have a better picture of what we might be up against. But we still have our fingers crossed that this fiasco will die down before Empress Catiz herself gets involved. </span'),
(60138,'/h2> The Amarr Empress has publicly declined to intervene officially in the territorial dispute between us and Kazar Numon. Sadly, she also expressly has not forbidden other Amarr Holders from acting privately in this matter. As a result, the Sarum lords who originally campaigned for intervention have ordered an outlying fleet of Imperial Navy ships to aid Numon anyway. They are led by an Imperial Fleet Commander who''s part of House Sarum, one Ishtai Sarum. We need to prevent him from moving his fleet into defensive positions around the area claimed by Numon. To do this, we must execute a number of hit-and-run attacks while they move through our territory. We''ve located what seems to be a reconnaissance team of theirs, en route to the dungeon. They are currently flying through the dungeon''s system, and we''d like you to intercept them immediately. Leave no survivors - we don''t want them reporting anything back to their commander. </span'),
(60139,'/h2> Our surveillance teams have reported a large force of Imperial Navy ships moving toward the dungeon. If we let them all arrive safely at their destination, we will have a very difficult fight on our hands: We need to weaken them before they have a chance to settle in and fortify themselves at their destination. Part of their fleet is currently in a deadspace pocket in the dungeon''s system. Their plan seems to be to move slowly between deadspace areas to prevent our heavy artillery from locking on to them. I want you to conduct an attack on the couple of squadrons that have already arrived at that deadspace pocket; I will provide you with bookmarks to the exact location. Speed is crucial for your success here. You need to strike them hard and fast and get out of there before they know what hit them. Tarry too long, and you''ll have the entire fleet on you. </span'),
(60073,'/h2> Our guerrilla tactics have worked well. The remainder of the Amarr fleet has reached its destination, but they are substantially weakened. Now it''s time to launch our final attack. The remaining forces have started to rebuild the defensive perimeter around the Numon claim. The remnants of Numon''s mercenary force guards the area now, along with the partial Navy fleet. Best, though, is the fact that Kazar, head of House Numon, has apparently decided to risk his own hide to defend his precious section of space. Killing him will be the icing on the cake for us. Your task is simple, you. Attack the Numon and Amarr forces head on, and obliterate them completely. Leave no survivors. But do bring me Numon''s head. It will make a nice souvenir. </span')
